<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Lemovices</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 51 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Gallic people of the Limousin who sent ten thousand men to relieve Alesia and whose name survives in Limoges.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Lemovices held the granite uplands of the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/massif-central">Massif Central</a>, in the modern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/viscounty-of-limoges">Limousin</a>. Caesar lists them among the allies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vercingetorix">Vercingetorix</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Their land was rich in gold, which was mined in many small workings before the Roman conquest. Their main oppidum was at Villejoubert, near Saint-Denis-des-Murs.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 52 BCE they sent ten thousand men to Alesia, and their leader Sedullus was killed there. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> their capital was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limoges">Augustoritum</a>, later Lemovices, from which come Limoges and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/viscounty-of-limoges">Limousin</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/lemovices.jpg" alt="Lemovices" width="320" height="307"><figcaption>Image: Mikl194VF · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Territoire_l%C3%A9movice.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 51 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Sedullus</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gaulish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-176&amp;focus=lemovices" aria-label="Lemovices on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4739 561 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lemovices lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5059 817h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5059 817h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day France. <a href="/atlas?year=-176&amp;focus=lemovices">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

